# ML experiment policy

## Temporal discipline

- Chronological, date-disjoint splits only. Never split a calendar date across partitions.
- `TRAIN_SEASONS = (2023, 2024)`. 2022 is prior-only context. 2025 is historical benchmark, never pristine. 2026 is locked retrospective / confirmatory only.
- Fit preprocessing on train dates only. Select on inner folds, confirm on distinct outer folds.

## Leakage rules

- Every feature must be known before first pitch. Forbidden as features: same-game K/PA/Outs/k_rate/actual TBF, current-game rolling contributions, future dates/seasons/lineups/park outcomes, raw IDs/names/teams/dates/join keys.
- Level 2 uses prior games only (exclude current-date games including doubleheaders). Park for season Y uses seasons < Y.
- `src/Python/features.py` + frozen registries gate which columns may train. Unknown numerics fail loudly.

## Experiment cards

- Plan before running: immutable hypothesis, comparator, population, temporal splits, metrics, slices, bootstrap unit, promotion rule, stop rule, input hashes, permitted deviations, output paths.
- Write under `research/offseason_2026/experiments/<card>/` with card + manifest + deviations. Never overwrite a prior card.
- Shadow first: new columns beside live, zero live-path change. Promote only via `champion_challenger_protocol.md` + `experiment_sop.md` with sign-off + revert path.

## No-2026-tuning

Do not retune floors, veto, Kelly, WS1c, Poisson, or champion from 2026 paper or juiced 2026 slices. Clean 2025-select / 2026-judge once, post-9/27, pre-registered.
